---
[consumers/golden-retriever] Fauxlden Retriever consumption exercise (started)
A synthetic whole-system description used to consume Grimoire before a real consumer exists. It stress-tests whether the language can describe arbitrary hot-path facts without making r3/r4 terminology, priorities, or mechanisms normative.
> Fauxlden Retriever is a test fixture, not a product consumer and not a source of layer priority.
> Use r3/r4 only to exercise the description language against a dense whole-system case; do not promote its vocabulary or architecture into Grimoire without an independent language need.
> The fixture includes whole-system facts such as tensors, passes, optimizer flags, gradient interventions, seeds, evidence artifacts, placement paths, bandwidth costs, and intentionally undefined behavior.
> R4 geometry is fixture evidence only: candidate plurality and multi-location reach are separate axes; each candidate lead contains a spacetime tube; every tube advances one frame; paired scoring reads all candidate spacetime; exactly one candidate is selected for execution.
---
[projlang/spec] Projection language specification (notstarted)
The sibling specification: select, invert, decorate; folding by join and chain; checks as cardinality expectations; definition-site opacity; symbolic values.
-> grammar/build
-> projlang/design
