[grammar/build] Grammar of the format (notstarted)
Formal productions for the whole data format: vocabulary graduated into grammar, addresses, core and layer documents, extension parameters, canonical serialization.
-> core/vocab-review
-> namespaces/minting
-> projlang/design
-> schemas/meta
> Built autonomously by Claude to satisfy the specification; lands at grammar/review.
> Gated on the vocabulary read-through rather than the full freeze, since productions graduate from vocabulary. Relax if wanted sooner.
@guidance text/markdown ./spec/grimoire.md
---
[core/freeze] Stamp the core spec (notstarted) @dispatch(mechanical)
Give the document its version. The spec mandates versioning for everything it touches; the stamp is the freeze.
-> core/vocab-review
> Revalidate the current specification and its version after the renewed vocabulary review.
@guidance text/markdown ./spec/grimoire.md
---
[core/vocab-review] Vocabulary read-through (notstarted)
Your deliberate read of the Vocabulary section: the definitions that graduate into productions, and the section that churned in every revision. The last human gate. Exclusively a human activity — never dispatched to an agent — performed only when the user explicitly delegates it (trigger phrase: "review and approve if appropriate").
-> core/spec
---
[core/spec] Core specification (reviewing)
The core data-format specification: pure data, definition sites and scoping, locality, extension parameters, and requirements on the projection language and layers.
@artifact text/markdown ./spec/grimoire.md
